INT. ROOFTOP GREENHOUSE - APARTMENT BLOCK - DAWN

A glass lean-to bolted to a tar roof, crowded with tomato vines and orchid pots. Gray light. Condensation drips from the panes. A fan turns slowly overhead.

DETECTIVE OSWALDO PEREIRA-LANE (50s, rumpled raincoat, thermos) stands over a body slumped between the tomato racks. The victim wears a gardener's apron and rubber boots.

At the door, patrolwoman SABINA KOWALCZYK (20s, rain cape) guards the entrance. Next to her stands the building super, MR. THADDEUS BRIGHTWATER (60s, keys on a ring, cardigan), wringing his cap.

On the far side of the glass, a nervous tenant, MISS HYACINTH LOVELACE (30s, silk robe, bare feet), watches from the stairwell.

                    OSWALDO
          Who found him?

                    THADDEUS
          I did, Detective. Came up to check the pipes.

                    OSWALDO
          What time?

                    THADDEUS
          Half past five.

Oswaldo crouches. A small trowel lies beside the body, clean. He lifts the victim's hand. The fingernails are packed with fresh soil.

                    OSWALDO
          (to Sabina)
          The roof door. Locked or unlocked?

                    SABINA
          Unlocked, sir.

                    OSWALDO
          Who has a key?

                    THADDEUS
          Just me. And Miss Lovelace. She waters the orchids.

All eyes shift to the stairwell. Hyacinth steps back into the shadows, then slowly forward again.

                    HYACINTH
          I was asleep.

                    OSWALDO
          Miss Lovelace, your feet are muddy.

She looks down. Pale mud streaks both soles. Oswaldo pours coffee from the thermos into its cap, sips, and says nothing for a long moment.
